WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.760
A room with the window wide open.

2
00:00:02.810 --> 00:00:06.820
One person rubs her arms
and says: it's cold in here.

3
00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:10.550
Without a word, the other
gets up and shuts the window.

4
00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:12.440
Now an empty room.

5
00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:15.600
Someone reads a thermometer
and says the same thing.

6
00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:17.090
Nobody moves.

7
00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:20.810
A request in one room, a
plain statement in the other.

8
00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:24.200
So how does the listener
know to shut the window?

9
00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:27.590
In this mission, you'll see that
words don't just say things.

10
00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:29.150
They do things.

11
00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:33.370
You'll meet four rules we quietly
expect every speaker to follow.

12
00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:35.530
Does anyone actually follow them?

13
00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:38.720
And you'll line up different
ways of asking for something,

14
00:00:38.770 --> 00:00:41.110
and ask which is the politest.

15
00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:45.250
Your mission: explain how the
listener knows to shut the window.
